In India, electronic records are legally recognized under Section 3 of the Information Technology Act, 2000 (IT Act). This section states that any document or record generated, stored, or transmitted electronically shall be deemed to be a record and shall be admissible as evidence in any court or other authority in India.

Additionally, Section 29 of the IT Act also provides that any electronic record shall be deemed to be a record and shall be admissible as evidence in any court or other authority in India, if it is:

* Made by a person having the capacity to make a record;
* Made by means of a device or machine;
* Made from any document or record;
* Made from any document or record, or from any electronic record;
* Made from any document or record, or from any electronic record, or from any document or record, or from any electronic record.

The IT Act also provides for the electronic filing of court cases and documents, which is governed by the Electronic Courts Rules, 2019.
